([06:38] Interviewer: [M2.2] Walk me through the last flight you planned, step by) Tj T*
(step, as it actually went.) Tj T*
([06:40] Priya Nair: First thing, I build the preliminary load plan off the) Tj T*
(booked figures, usually around T-120. Takes me about twenty minutes.) Tj T*
([07:55] Priya Nair: For widebodies, honestly only me and one other controller) Tj T*
(really know the configurations.) Tj T*
([14:05] Priya Nair: Then I check special loads, dangerous goods and live) Tj T*
(animals, against the checklist. The notification from the cargo terminal often) Tj T*
(comes late.) Tj T*
([16:22] Priya Nair: If something can't be accepted, the airline decides what to) Tj T*
(offload. That takes anywhere from fifteen to forty minutes. Then I re-plan.) Tj T*
([21:45] Interviewer: How long did each part take, and where were you waiting on) Tj T*
(someone or something?) Tj T*
([21:50] Priya Nair: Ramp loads the aircraft, forty minutes or so, and sends back) Tj T*
(the loading report. It's still on paper and I re-key it. We sometimes wait) Tj T*
(fifteen minutes for it, and at peak we're short of containers.) Tj T*
([22:30] Priya Nair: Officially the ramp should send the report within ten) Tj T*
ET
